#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1035 expect=skipped domain=DS
#note "FLIPPED noViolation -> skipped by Fix #331 (M2-D24 bucket 2, owner ruling 2026-08-22). DSCAT is absent; under Fix #330 a bare empty(DSCAT) is TRUE on every row of an absent column (absent = all-missing) and nothing else in the Check restricts the rows, so the rule would flood -- the ruled disposition is Requirements.Variables.All [DSCAT], an auditable SKIP naming DSCAT as the reason, with the absence itself left to one presence rule. If this EXECUTES (violation or silent pass), the gate has been removed -- escalate, do not rewrite. History, before Fix #330: Absent-column fold: DSCAT is not declared at all. The bare `empty(DSCAT)` would broadcast-fold to TRUE over an absent column, but the loader-injected `var_exists(\"DSCAT\")` conjunct folds FALSE first and short-circuits the AND, so the rule executes and finds nothing (DSCAT is core=Exp, so no Requirements.Variables gate is authored). If this fires 1 violation at row=1, the guard has changed -- escalate, do not edit."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 2 | COMPLETED                 | COMPLETED
